description:
## Goal

Move the remaining non-coverage warning producer onto supported diagnostic facts and delete the global warning-once queue and flush lifecycle.

## Scope

The remaining production warning is type/numeric-literal-widened from type resolution. Its evidence belongs to the exact demanded resolution attempt and immutable source provenance that observed the numeric literal. Reproduction replaces the attempt contribution; loss of demand or accepted-source replacement retracts it; independent supporters preserve it.

Rendering reads the current settled diagnostic projection. A cached unchanged request still receives the current warning snapshot without rerunning resolution, while an unrelated edit wakes nothing.

## TDD

Prove first:

- first demanded numeric-literal type resolution publishes one warning fact;
- an undemanded declaration stays cold and produces none;
- identical requests return the current warning without new jobs, wakes, allocations, or telemetry emission from producers;
- relevant replacement removes, moves, or restores the warning exactly;
- rejected replacement preserves the accepted warning and provenance;
- two demanders retain shared warning support until the last leaves;
- location-only replacement updates only diagnostic provenance;
- ordering is deterministic under FIFO/LIFO/permutation.

## Required deletion

Delete World.reported_warnings, World.warning_diagnostics, WarningDiagnosticKey, clear_reported_warnings, note_warning_once, emit_warning_once, flush_reported_warnings, and every drive/product-drive warning flush. Warning rendering must not be a queue drain, side effect, retry registry, or whole-World scan. Keep Diagnostic as presentation data, not authority.

Update resolver, diagnostic, fact-engine, pipeline, telemetry, and user-facing documentation in the same commit. Full focused, causal, replacement, fixture, CLI, formatting, check, and strict-Clippy gates pass.
